Alright — here’s the complete beginner-friendly setup for LM Studio step-by-step on Windows.

We’ll do this like a fresh setup with no assumptions.


---

STEP 1 — Check Your Laptop Specs

First check:

RAM

GPU

Free storage


Press:

Windows + R

Type:

dxdiag

Press Enter.

Check:

Memory (RAM)

GPU name



---

Important

For:

qwen2.5-coder:32b

Recommended:

32GB RAM

NVIDIA GPU preferred

25GB free storage


If you have:

16GB RAM → better use 14B model first.



---

STEP 2 — Download LM Studio

Open browser.

Go to:

LM Studio Download

Click:

Download for Windows

Wait for download.


---

STEP 3 — Install LM Studio

Open downloaded file.

Usually named something like:

LM-Studio-Setup.exe

Then:

Click Next

Accept terms

Install

Finish



---

STEP 4 — Open LM Studio

Press Windows key.

Search:

LM Studio

Open it.

First launch may take some time.


---

STEP 5 — Understand The Interface

You’ll see left sidebar:

Section	Meaning

Chat	Where you talk to AI
Discover	Download AI models
My Models	Models you downloaded
Developer	Advanced features



---

STEP 6 — Download Your AI Model

Click:

Discover

Search:

qwen2.5-coder

You’ll see many versions.


---

STEP 7 — Choose Correct Model

If You Have 32GB RAM

Choose:

Qwen2.5-Coder-32B-Instruct-GGUF

Then choose:

Q4_K_M


---

If You Have 16GB RAM

Choose:

Qwen2.5-Coder-14B-Instruct-GGUF

Then:

Q4_K_M


---

STEP 8 — Download Model

Click:

Download

Wait patiently.

Large models can take:

10–60 mins depending on internet.



---

STEP 9 — Load The Model

After download: go to:

Chat

Top dropdown: select your model.

Then click:

Load Model

Wait.

First startup may take:

1–3 minutes.



---

STEP 10 — Start Chatting

Type:

Explain Docker networking simply

OR:

Create Go REST API example

OR:

Create Jenkins pipeline for Python app

You now have local AI running on your laptop.


---

STEP 11 — Speed Improvements (IMPORTANT)

Go:

Settings

Then:

Runtime

Enable:

GPU Acceleration

CUDA/Vulkan if available


This makes responses much faster.


---

STEP 12 — Recommended Beginner Settings

Context Length

Set:

8192

Temperature

Set:

0.7


---

